  "notes": "Used for birds, reptiles, fish, insects, and other egg-laying animals. Also functions as a suru verb ({孵化|ふか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧). Sometimes used figuratively for business incubation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {孵化|ふか}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ — to hatch\n- {孵化|ふか}{器|き} — incubator\n- {孵化|ふか}⟦{率|りつ}→率：03802_ritsu⟧ — hatching rate\n- ⟦{人工|じんこう}→人工：11573_jinkou⟧{孵化|ふか} — artificial incubation\n- {孵化|ふか}⟦{直後|ちょくご}→直後：04525_chokugo⟧ — immediately after hatching\n\nUSAGE:\nIn business contexts, {孵化|ふか} is sometimes used metaphorically, similar to English \"incubation.\" An インキュベーター (incubator) supports new businesses, paralleling how an {孵化|ふか}{器|き} supports eggs.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{羽化|うか}→羽化：18950_uka⟧ — emergence (of an insect from pupa to adult)\n- ⟦{産卵|さんらん}→産卵：13565_sanran⟧ — egg-laying, spawning",
